# Test write policy

Read application source (`app/`, `src/`, and similar) to learn behavior. Do not edit it.

Write only:

- `test/**`
- `vitest.config.ts`
- `playwright.config.ts`
- root `README.md`
- `.gitignore`
- `AGENTS.md`
- `.cursor/skills/**`
- `.cursor/agents/**`

Git and GitHub CLI (`gh`) commands are allowed, including commit, push, and pull requests.

Unit tests go in `test/unit`. Integration tests go in `test/integration`. End-to-end specs, plans, and page objects go in `test/e2e`. There are no frontend or backend test directories.

If a test fails because the product is wrong, change the test expectation only when the test was wrong. Otherwise report the product bug. Do not patch application source to make a test pass.

Call the `qa` role. For unit or integration tests, read the Vitest skill and follow only the UI or API section the prompt needs. For end-to-end tests, read the Playwright skill, then only the planner, generator, or healer tool the prompt asks for.
